      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.567,
          "end": 4.09,
          "en": "So by now, we already learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.09,
          "end": 7.58,
          "en": "about transitions, to transition component, what it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.58,
          "end": 9.34,
          "en": "and how you may use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.34,
          "end": 14.21,
          "en": "Sometimes you'll also want to run some JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.21,
          "end": 16.76,
          "en": "either as part of the transition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.76,
          "end": 20.3,
          "en": "maybe to even control the entire transition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.3,
          "end": 23.18,
          "en": "and the style changes Fruit JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.18,
          "end": 26.06,
          "en": "or maybe because you want to do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.06,
          "end": 30.01,
          "en": "when an animation starts or when it ends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.01,
          "end": 34,
          "en": "And vue gives you an opportunity to do that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34,
          "end": 36.25,
          "en": "It gives you various events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.25,
          "end": 39.94,
          "en": "which are emitted by this transition component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.94,
          "end": 41.71,
          "en": "during a transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.71,
          "end": 43.35,
          "en": "So when the transition starts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 46.51,
          "en": "when an element is added or when an element is removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.51,
          "end": 48.13,
          "en": "from the Dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.13,
          "end": 51.91,
          "en": "and I will show it here on this transition wrapping,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.91,
          "end": 53.41,
          "en": "this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.41,
          "end": 55.46,
          "en": "We can listen to various events here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.46,
          "end": 59.77,
          "en": "with v-on or the short and, the @ symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.77,
          "end": 62.29,
          "en": "and the first event to which we can list here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.29,
          "end": 64.67,
          "en": "is before-enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.67,
          "end": 68.2,
          "en": "Here, we can run a code which will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.2,
          "end": 71.63,
          "en": "when the element which is wrapped, this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.63,
          "end": 74.43,
          "en": "in this case is about to enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 77.77,
          "en": "So when the enter animation starts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.77,
          "end": 79.91,
          "en": "so in the end, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.91,
          "end": 84.91,
          "en": "this runs whenever this enter from CSS class is being added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.7,
          "end": 89.65,
          "en": "So right at the beginning, when the element is added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.65,
          "end": 91.473,
          "en": "and the animation starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.75999999999999,
          "end": 94.95,
          "en": "Now, I'll add a couple of methods here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.95,
          "end": 97.97,
          "en": "which allow us to print something to the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.97,
          "end": 101.50999999999999,
          "en": "so that we can see this all in action in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.50999999999999,
          "end": 104.163,
          "en": "And here I have beforeEnter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107,
          "end": 108.78,
          "en": "now this method name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.78,
          "end": 111.67,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be beforeEnter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.67,
          "end": 115.75,
          "en": "Here, adjust once to console.log beforeEnter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.75,
          "end": 119.533,
          "en": "So that we see that we uh, reached this event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 124.64,
          "en": "Now we can point at beforeEnter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.64,
          "end": 128.12,
          "en": "at this newly added method on the beforeEnter event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.12,
          "end": 129.9,
          "en": "Again, the method name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 132.24,
          "en": "The event name isn't beforeEnter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 134.94,
          "en": "it's one of the built in events transition emits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 139.81,
          "en": "and if we saved that and we opened the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.81,
          "end": 142.87,
          "en": "with the JavaScript console here in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.87,
          "end": 144.98,
          "en": "if I click toggle paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.98,
          "end": 148.39,
          "en": "we see beforeEnter being printed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.39,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "So that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 152.03,
          "en": "Now, if I remove the paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.03,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "we don't see beforeEnter again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 157.82,
          "en": "because it's only firing when the element enters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.82,
          "end": 160.263,
          "en": "So when the enter animation is played.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 165.82,
          "en": "Of course, we can also listen to the leaving though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.82,
          "end": 170.35,
          "en": "with @before-leave just as we have beforeEnter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.35,
          "end": 175.34,
          "en": "we can also listen to that event or the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.34,
          "end": 179.163,
          "en": "when that element that is wrapped is leaving the Dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.45,
          "end": 185.45,
          "en": "So here we can also add a before-Leave method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.872,
          "end": 190.123,
          "en": "where we then console.log beforeLeave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.77,
          "end": 194.93,
          "en": "Well, and of course we can now point at this method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.93,
          "end": 197.923,
          "en": "on our @before-leave event handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.09,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "If we saved this, reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 205.18,
          "en": "if I click toggle paragraph, we've got beforeEnter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.18,
          "end": 207.693,
          "en": "if I click it again, we got beforeLeave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.78,
          "end": 215.5,
          "en": "Now you actually also get an argument in those methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.5,
          "end": 217.09,
          "en": "automatically by vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.09,
          "end": 221.45,
          "en": "And that is the element hence we'll name it {el} here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.45,
          "end": 223.85,
          "en": "on which this animation runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.85,
          "end": 228.85,
          "en": "If I console.log{el} here and also here in beforeLeave",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 235.23,
          "en": "and save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.23,
          "end": 237.69,
          "en": "you will notice the difficulty toggle paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 237.69,
          "end": 239.21,
          "en": "It's printing the paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.21,
          "end": 242.35,
          "en": "which was added at the same for removing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.35,
          "end": 245.16,
          "en": "So if you need to do something with that element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.16,
          "end": 248.78,
          "en": "for example, change its styling In case you want to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.78,
          "end": 250.9,
          "en": "the Animation Fruit JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.9,
          "end": 252.68,
          "en": "something we're going to do in the next lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.68,
          "end": 255.68,
          "en": "by the way, then you can do this with help of the element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.68,
          "end": 258.41,
          "en": "which you get automatically as argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.41,
          "end": 262.187,
          "en": "when listening to beforeEnter and beforeLeave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.09,
          "end": 267.37,
          "en": "But beforeEnter and beforeLeave is not everything we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.37,
          "end": 271.49,
          "en": "We also have an @enter event to which we can listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 271.49,
          "end": 276.49,
          "en": "This is basically the equivalent to the Active CSS Class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.17,
          "end": 280.88,
          "en": "The enter event is triggered as a next step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.927,
          "end": 285.15,
          "en": "then beforeEnter is done, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 285.15,
          "end": 287.86,
          "en": "Now here, I want to trigger an enter method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.86,
          "end": 291.57,
          "en": "which doesn't exist yet, but which I'll of course add now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.57,
          "end": 294.34000000000003,
          "en": "Here, let's say I add, enter()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.34000000000003,
          "end": 298.65,
          "en": "and I console.log(enter) here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.65,
          "end": 300.61,
          "en": "We also get the element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.61,
          "end": 302.69,
          "en": "So it would be also we could interact with it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 302.69,
          "end": 305.137,
          "en": "If we wanted to enable console.log(el).",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 306.04,
          "end": 308.07,
          "en": "If we now saved it and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.07,
          "end": 312.26,
          "en": "if I toggle the paragraph we see beforeEnter first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 312.26,
          "end": 315.993,
          "en": "and the paragraph, and then we see enter and the paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.94,
          "end": 318.98,
          "en": "And of course we can also listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 318.98,
          "end": 323.98,
          "en": "to when the animation finishes with @after-enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 324.91,
          "end": 328.173,
          "en": "And here, I want to trigger an afterEnter method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 329.185,
          "end": 330.23,
          "en": "which we have yet to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 330.23,
          "end": 332.77,
          "en": "This will fire whenever the animation is done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.77,
          "end": 335.15,
          "en": "the entering animation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 335.15,
          "end": 340.15,
          "en": "So here, I will add an afterEnter method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 341.78,
          "end": 345.02,
          "en": "console.log (afterEnter)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 346.09000000000003,
          "end": 348.45,
          "en": "and here we also get the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 348.45,
          "end": 353.45,
          "en": "So if I print that here, saved it and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 354.52,
          "end": 356.35,
          "en": "click toggle paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 356.35,
          "end": 359.01,
          "en": "you see, we got beforeEnter first, then enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 359.01,
          "end": 361.1,
          "en": "and then afterEnter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 361.1,
          "end": 362.79,
          "en": "Now we have a quick animation here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 362.79,
          "end": 366.65,
          "en": "So it looked like afterEnter was basically called directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.65,
          "end": 368.04,
          "en": "after enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 368.04,
          "end": 370.65,
          "en": "but actually it waits for the animation to finish",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 370.65,
          "end": 372.62,
          "en": "until afterEnter gets called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 372.62,
          "end": 375.7,
          "en": "And I can show this by going to .para-enter-active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 375.7,
          "end": 378.563,
          "en": "and ramping this up to two seconds, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.53,
          "end": 382.68,
          "en": "Keep in mind that vue will read this duration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 382.68,
          "end": 384.77,
          "en": "Vue analyzes this duration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 384.77,
          "end": 387.48,
          "en": "and it knows how long the animation will take.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 387.48,
          "end": 390.153,
          "en": "It will add the CSS classes appropriately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 390.153,
          "end": 394.49,
          "en": "and it will also trigger those events appropriately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 394.49,
          "end": 399.09000000000003,
          "en": "And now afterEnter will only be called after two seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 399.09000000000003,
          "end": 401.013,
          "en": "when the animation completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 403.15999999999997,
          "end": 405.68,
          "en": "So now if I reload here and click toggle paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 405.68,
          "end": 407.15,
          "en": "we only see enter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 407.15,
          "end": 408.475,
          "en": "and only after two seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 408.475,
          "end": 411.57,
          "en": "we see after enter being printed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 411.57,
          "end": 415.253,
          "en": "because that only is called when the animation finishes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 417.2,
          "end": 419.98,
          "en": "And of course we have the equivalence for removing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 419.98,
          "end": 422.8,
          "en": "I'll restructure this to make it a bit easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 422.8,
          "end": 425.02,
          "en": "We already added beforeLeave",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 425.02,
          "end": 427.15,
          "en": "but of course we now also have \"leave\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 427.15,
          "end": 431.24,
          "en": "where I want to call @leave method and @after-leave",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 431.24,
          "end": 434.3,
          "en": "which is called when the \"leave\" transition finished,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 434.3,
          "end": 437.84,
          "en": "here, I want to call an afterLeave method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
